## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Nepal Agriculture Dashboard project.

### Changes Made

**Modified Files:**
1. `package.json` - Added `@vercel/speed-insights` v2.0.0 dependency
2. `pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated with new package and its dependencies
3. `src/App.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component integration

### Implementation Details

**1. Package Installation:**
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using pnpm
- Package manager: pnpm v10.15.0

**2. Component Integration:**
- Imported `SpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to App.tsx, placed alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component
- The component is positioned at the root level of the application, inside the `<BrowserRouter>` wrapper, ensuring it tracks all page navigation and performance metrics

**3. Framework Configuration:**
- Project: React + Vite
- Following official Vercel documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
- Used React-specific import path: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`

### Verification Completed

All verification steps completed successfully:
✅ TypeScript type checking passed (tsc --noEmit)
✅ ESLint linting passed with 0 warnings
✅ Production build successful (1.25s build time)
✅ All 30 tests passed across 7 test files

### Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically:
- Track Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, etc.)
- Collect real user performance metrics
- Make data available in the Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights section
- Deploy tracking script routes at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*`

No additional configuration is required. The integration follows the same pattern as the existing Vercel Analytics setup in the project.
